A self-signed RSA certificate signed with RSASSA-PSS: the hash is in the AlgorithmIdentifier's
parameters, not its OID, so this is what makes x509Pss report `rsaPssSha256 rather than `unknown.

openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout /dev/null -noenc -sha256 \
  -sigopt rsa_padding_mode:pss -sigopt rsa_pss_saltlen:32 -sigopt rsa_mgf1_md:sha256 \
  -not_before 20260101000000Z -not_after 20360101000000Z -set_serial 0x7b \
  -subj "/CN=pss.neant.test" \
  -addext "subjectAltName=DNS:pss.neant.test" \
  -addext "basicConstraints=critical,CA:FALSE" \
  -out tests/data/selfsigned-pss.pem

